E["npc:donova-snowden"] = {t="npc",n="Donova Snowden",z="winterspring",s="Beside Frostfire Hot Springs, Donova Snowden studies Winterspring’s strange warmth and the Winterfall furbolgs’ growing corruption. She camps in the bitter cold, far from most travelers in Everlook.",h="Beside Frostfire Hot Springs, Donova Snowden studies Winterspring’s strange warmth and the Winterfall...",sec={{t="A Lone Researcher in the Snow",b="Donova Snowden camps in the frozen wilds near Frostfire Hot Springs, while most travelers stay in Everlook. She studies heat rising through the permafrost and dark influences spreading among Winterspring’s native wildlife. Practical and determined, she calls on passing adventurers from both the Alliance and the Horde to gather samples and help curb local threats.",sp=0},{t="Investigating the Winterfall",b="Donova Snowden studies the Winterfall furbolgs, whose behavior has grown erratic and aggressive. She examines potent brews such as Winterfall Firewater and strange toxins circulating among the tribes, seeking the cause of their sudden madness. Her fieldwork makes her a key contact for anyone trying to understand the corruption spreading through the northern mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Donova Snowden?",a="Donova Snowden camps beside a small hot spring southwest of Frostfire Hot Springs, across the main road, in Winterspring.",al={"donova snowden location","where is donova","donova snowden map"}},{q="Why is Donova out here in the freezing cold?",a="Donova Snowden studies Winterspring’s unusual hot springs and investigates the corruption affecting the local Winterfall furbolg tribe.",al={"why is donova in winterspring","donova snowden purpose"}},{q="Will Donova work with Horde players?",a="Yes. Though she is a dwarf, Donova Snowden works independently and offers work to Alliance and Horde adventurers alike.",al={"is donova alliance only","can horde talk to donova","donova snowden faction"}},{q="What is Donova investigating regarding the Winterfall furbolgs?",a="Donova Snowden studies the corruption driving the Winterfall tribe to madness. She investigates their strange brews, including Winterfall Firewater, and the foul toxins found among their runners.",al={"donova furbolg quest","winterfall firewater research"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize the urge to brave frozen peaks alone. Donova Snowden’s fieldwork recalls the dwarven appetite for exploration far from Khaz Modan.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can work with Donova Snowden despite her dwarven heritage. She sets faction allegiance aside to recruit capable scouts against Winterspring’s wild beasts and corrupted furbolgs."},kw={"donova snowden","firewater","frostfire hot springs","furbolg","researcher","winterfall","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","subzone:frostfire-hot-springs","topic:dwarf"},src={"Donova Snowden"}}
E["npc:rivern-frostwind"] = {t="npc",n="Rivern Frostwind",z="winterspring",s="At Frostsaber Rock, Rivern Frostwind trains riders and guards Winterspring's frostsabers. His frost tiger Glacier is at his side, and only the most dedicated Alliance champions earn the honor of riding one.",h="At Frostsaber Rock, Rivern Frostwind trains riders and guards Winterspring's frostsabers.",sec={{t="Master of the Frostsabers",b="From icy Frostsaber Rock, Rivern Frostwind oversees the breeding and care of Winterspring frostsabers. Unlike the nightsabers of Teldrassil and Ashenvale, these cats are bred to endure northern Kalimdor's bitter cold.\n\nRivern entrusts a saber only to those who prove their commitment to protecting the beasts. They must gather fresh meat from the tundra, clear out Winterfall furbolgs, and drive back rampaging frost giants before he deems them worthy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rivern Frostwind?",a="At Frostsaber Rock, Rivern Frostwind is a night elf riding master and caretaker of the Wintersaber Trainers faction. With his tiger Glacier, he protects and properly rears Winterspring's powerful native big cats.",al={"rivern frostwind lore","frostsaber trainer","who is rivern"}},{q="Why is he in Winterspring?",a="Rivern lives at Frostsaber Rock to train riders and safeguard the region's rare white frostsabers. Aggressive Winterfall furbolgs, encroaching giants, and harsh conditions threaten the predators, so he keeps order and looks after their well-being.",al={"why is rivern here","frostsaber rock purpose"}},{q="Can Horde players work with Rivern?",a="No. Rivern Frostwind is loyal to the night elves and the Alliance. He refuses to deal with Horde travelers at Frostsaber Rock and reserves his trust and mount training for Alliance champions.",al={"can horde get wintersaber","rivern horde friendly"}},{q="Who is the tiger beside him?",a="Glacier is the frost tiger beside Rivern. He is Rivern's personal companion and a fine example of the hardy cats native to the Winterspring tundra.",al={"who is glacier","rivern frostwind tiger"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Rivern Frostwind is the sole provider of the rare Winterspring Frostsaber. Riders beyond Darnassus can earn the chance to tame one of Kalimdor's fiercest beasts through perseverance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know nightsabers are closely tied to Elune's priesthood and Kalimdor's sentinels. Rivern's frostsabers belong to an adapted, solitary lineage bred for Winterspring's harsh snowscapes."},kw={"frostsaber rock","glacier","mount trainer","rivern frostwind","wintersaber trainers","winterspring frostsaber"},rel={"subzone:frostsaber-rock","zone:winterspring","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Rivern Frostwind"}}
E["subzone:darkwhisper-gorge"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkwhisper Gorge",z="winterspring",s="Demons hold Darkwhisper Gorge in the southern heights of Winterspring. They fled there after Archimonde fell and now guard its minerals and planar relics.",h="Demons hold Darkwhisper Gorge in the southern heights of Winterspring.",sec={{t="A Legion Foothold in the Snow",b="In Winterspring's southern heights, demons have made Darkwhisper Gorge their refuge. After Archimonde fell atop Mount Hyjal, the survivors scattered into the mountain ranges. A disciplined vanguard settled here and made the border a stronghold.\n\nHederine demons lead the foothold under Lady Hederine. Manastalkers, slayers, and initiates defend the tunnels and fiery camps. At the gorge's lowest point, a sealed archway hints at passages higher into the sacred mountain.",sp=0},{t="Hidden Reagents and Rare Knowledge",b="Danger has not kept adventurers and opportunists from the gorge's wealth. Its ravines hold truesilver and dense thorium deposits. In the shadowed grottos, the imp vendor Vi'el sells fel-tainted reagents such as felcloth and gromsblood.\n\nThe elusive high elf Earthcaller Franzahl holds ancient metallurgical lore about smelting rare elementium.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many demons in Winterspring?",a="Demons in Darkwhisper Gorge survived the Burning Legion's invasion of Mount Hyjal during the Third War. After Archimonde fell at the World Tree, his broken forces retreated into the chasms to regroup.",al={"why demons here","darkwhisper legion lore","where did the demons come from"}},{q="What is the sealed gate at the back of the gorge?",a="A runed archway and an active magical barrier stand deep in the gorge's southern depths. They guard a mountain pass leading straight to Mount Hyjal.",al={"darkwhisper portal","instance portal winterspring","hyjal gate"}},{q="Who leads the demons here?",a="The Hederine, a sect of demonic invaders, dominate the encampment under Lady Hederine's apparent command. They patrol the ravines with slayers, initiates, and fell hounds called manastalkers.",al={"darkwhisper boss","hederine leader","who rules darkwhisper"}},{q="Why would an adventurer venture into Darkwhisper Gorge?",a="Darkwhisper Gorge is exceptionally dangerous, and groups must work together to cross it safely. Warlocks seek planar bindings, priests hunt the rare Eye of Shadow, and blacksmiths and miners seek rich thorium veins. Scholars come looking for Earthcaller Franzahl.",al={"why go to darkwhisper","darkwhisper quests","darkwhisper rewards"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Hederine demons in these caverns hold vital planar components. The gorge tests warlocks who seek mastery of greater summoning rituals such as the Doomguard.",["profession:Mining"]="The perilous chasms hold abundant truesilver and rich thorium veins. Miners brave enough to slip past elite demons can reach them."},kw={"burning legion","darkwhisper gorge","earthcaller franzahl","eye of shadow","hederine","lady hederine","mount hyjal","vi'el","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","subzone:frostwhisper-gorge","topic:burning-legion","topic:third-war","zone:blastedlands"},src={"Darkwhisper Gorge"}}
E["subzone:dun-mandarr"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Mandarr",z="winterspring",s="In southeastern Winterspring, enraged moonkin guard the abandoned dwarven camp of Dun Mandarr.",h="In southeastern Winterspring, enraged moonkin guard the abandoned dwarven camp of Dun Mandarr.",sec={{t="A Forsaken Camp",b="Dun Mandarr lies in Winterspring’s frozen southeastern reaches. Jaron Stoneshaper made his camp there, and uncovered the Blue-Feathered Amulet. The discovery roused the native wildkin to fury. They swept down on the camp and drove the dwarves away. Now moonkin prowl the broken shelters and guard the cavern. No friendly souls remain among the snowbanks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the camp at Dun Mandarr?",a="Dwarf explorer Jaron Stoneshaper built the camp at Dun Mandarr. While excavating, he uncovered the Blue-Feathered Amulet, rousing the surrounding wildkin to attack. Jaron and his companions fled, leaving the camp abandoned and overrun.",al={"why is dun mandarr abandoned","who built dun mandarr","what is dun mandarr"}},{q="Why are there so many moonkin here?",a="The local wildkin hold the cavern and surrounding relics sacred. When Jaron Stoneshaper excavated the Blue-Feathered Amulet, they flew into a violent frenzy to reclaim it and defend their territory. They drove out the intruders and took over the camp.",al={"why are there wildkin here","dun mandarr owlbeasts","why are owlbeasts attacking"}},{q="Where did Jaron Stoneshaper go?",a="After rampaging moonkin drove Jaron Stoneshaper from his camp, he retreated elsewhere in Winterspring. There, he regrouped and sought aid in recovering his stolen research and gear.",al={"where is jaron stoneshaper","jaron stoneshaper location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the traditional dwarven prefix in Dun Mandarr’s name. The ruined site reminds you that archaeological ambition in ancient Kalimdor can end in disaster.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the moonkin guarding Dun Mandarr fiercely protect natural and celestial artifacts. They react violently when outsiders disturb sacred relics such as the Blue-Feathered Amulet."},kw={"blue-feathered amulet","dun mandarr","dwarf camp","jaron stoneshaper","moonkin","wildkin","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring"},src={"Dun Mandarr"}}
E["subzone:everlook"] = {t="subzone",n="Everlook",z="winterspring",s="Everlook shelters travelers at the meeting of Winterspring’s routes. The Steamwheedle Cartel keeps this northern outpost open to merchants, prospectors, and researchers, offering a neutral refuge from the high-altitude cold.",h="Everlook shelters travelers at the meeting of Winterspring’s routes.",sec={{t="Commerce at the Edge of the World",b="At Winterspring’s crossroads, Everlook is the Steamwheedle Cartel’s northernmost outpost. Like Gadgetzan and Booty Bay, it is a walled settlement beneath permafrost. Alliance and Horde travelers find warmth and shelter here because the town keeps strict neutrality. Its bank and shared auction house are the region’s only operational ones. Hired bruisers guard the settlement, where travelers seek refuge from ferocious frostsabers and yetis.",sp=0},{t="Gears in the Tundra",b="Everlook’s icy wooden roofs and whimsical penguin wallpaper shelter workshops for engineering and advanced alchemical laboratories. Goblin tinkerers pursue their craft away from prying eyes.\n\nThe Argent Dawn recently sent Gregor Greystone to negotiate with town leadership. The order watches the region’s ancient ruins and gathering northern threats with care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Everlook?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel owns and operates Everlook. The Argent Dawn sent Gregor Greystone as its representative.",al={"who runs everlook","everlook leader","who is in charge of everlook"}},{q="Why is Everlook safe for both Alliance and Horde?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel enforces strict commercial neutrality. Goblin bruisers quickly pummel anyone who starts a fight, leaving travelers of every allegiance free to trade.",al={"is everlook neutral","can horde and alliance visit everlook","everlook pvp rules"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn in Everlook?",a="The Argent Dawn keeps an official presence in Everlook through its emissary, Gregor Greystone. He represents the order to the goblin merchants and watches for local threats.",al={"what is argent dawn doing here","gregor greystone everlook","argent dawn winterspring"}},{q="Where does Everlook get its trade goods?",a="Everlook’s trade goods arrive by trade flights and surface caravans along Winterspring’s main trade routes. Those routes meet at the outpost.",al={"everlook smuggling","winterspring trade goods","where do everlook goods come from"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Everlook is a major hub for high-level engineers, especially those who specialize in goblin engineering. They can learn to build a dimensional ripper keyed directly to the settlement."},kw={"everlook","goblin","gregor greystone","snow","steamwheedle cartel","trade outpost","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","topic:goblin","zone:felwood","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:argent-dawn"},src={"Everlook"}}
E["subzone:frostfire-hot-springs"] = {t="subzone",n="Frostfire Hot Springs",z="winterspring",s="Steam rises from Frostfire Hot Springs beneath the snow of western Winterspring. Curious scholars and hardy fishers come despite the cold, while hostile furbolgs keep near the pools.",h="Steam rises from Frostfire Hot Springs beneath the snow of western Winterspring.",sec={{t="Steaming Waters in the Snow",b="Near the tunnel to Timbermaw Hold, warm water runs beneath the snow at Frostfire Hot Springs. No one knows what keeps it hot. Winterfall furbolgs roam the banks, and their aggression makes the pools dangerous to approach. Fishers who brave the furbolgs and the winter chill find rare open water where fish thrive.",sp=0},{t="A Geothermal Mystery",b="The springs draw curious observers who wonder how their waters stay hot in this frozen land. Donova Snowden, an inquisitive dwarf, keeps a lonely vigil nearby as she studies their origin and composition. She suspects the heat may not be natural. Dark magic from the demonic stronghold of Darkwhisper Gorge could be seeping north and stirring the waters underground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there hot springs in freezing Winterspring?",a="No one knows what heats the springs. Donova Snowden is investigating whether demonic influence from Darkwhisper Gorge may be involved.",al={"why is water hot","frostfire origin","hot water winterspring"}},{q="Who is Donova Snowden?",a="Donova Snowden is a dwarven researcher camped near the hot springs. She studies their unusual properties and seeks travelers’ help in understanding Winterspring’s dangers.",al={"dwarf near springs","donova snowden lore","hot springs questgiver"}},{q="Could the springs be tied to demonic magic?",a="Donova Snowden suspects demonic corruption from Darkwhisper Gorge, far to the south, may run deep through the earth. It could heat or alter underground currents that rise at Frostfire Hot Springs.",al={"demon hot springs","darkwhisper connection","corrupted water"}},{q="Who lives around the hot springs?",a="Aggressive Winterfall furbolgs hold territory near the springs and attack outsiders on sight. Stay alert around the pools.",al={"frostfire enemies","who controls hot springs","furbolgs hot springs"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize your kin’s curiosity in Donova Snowden. She braves the frozen elements to study geological mysteries.",["class:Druid"]="The springs’ unexplained warmth and unusual properties raise questions about the forces beneath Winterspring."},kw={"darkwhisper gorge","donova snowden","frostfire hot springs","timbermaw hold","winterfall","winterspring"},rel={"npc:donova-snowden","zone:winterspring","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:darkwhisper-gorge"},src={"Frostfire Hot Springs"}}
E["subzone:frostsaber-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Frostsaber Rock",z="winterspring",s="Frostsabers find shelter and training at Frostsaber Rock in northern Winterspring. Its stone rise overlooks the region’s snowy reaches.",h="Frostsabers find shelter and training at Frostsaber Rock in northern Winterspring.",sec={{t="A Perch in the Tundra",b="Frostsaber Rock rises over Winterspring’s frozen northern wilds. Frostsabers prowl its slopes and valleys. At the summit, Rivern Frostwind, a solitary night elf, raises and tends the cats. Alliance champions who brave the harsh conditions and prove their devotion may earn the rare privilege of learning to raise, tame, and ride one of these snowy mounts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives atop Frostsaber Rock?",a="Rivern Frostwind camps at the summit and trains the frostsaber cats of the region. Alliance members seeking a frostsaber companion can look to him as a mentor.",al={"who is at frostsaber rock","frostsaber rock trainer","rivern location"}},{q="Can Horde players train beasts here?",a="No. Rivern Frostwind offers training and companion beasts only to trusted Alliance allies. Horde travelers find no welcome at the summit.",al={"horde frostsaber rock","can horde get frostsaber","rivern horde"}},{q="What creatures are found around the rock?",a="Wild frostsaber cats roam the icy crag and nearby plateaus. Other hardy beasts native to Winterspring’s harsh climate live there as well.",al={"what lives here","frostsaber rock beasts","frostsabers in winterspring"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you can earn Rivern Frostwind’s trust atop the rock and begin the arduous training needed to ride the famed Winterspring frostsaber.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can observe some of northern Kalimdor’s fiercest native predators on the crag and its surrounding slopes."},kw={"alliance mount","frostsaber","frostsaber rock","rivern frostwind","wintersaber","winterspring"},rel={"npc:rivern-frostwind","zone:winterspring","topic:alliance"},src={"Frostsaber Rock"}}
E["subzone:frostwhisper-gorge"] = {t="subzone",n="Frostwhisper Gorge",z="winterspring",s="In southern Winterspring, Frostwhisper Gorge runs just north of Darkwhisper Gorge. Ancient night elven ruins lie across its icy floor and cliffs, now held by Frostmaul giants. A lone dwarf camp overlooks the ocean from the eastern rim.",h="In southern Winterspring, Frostwhisper Gorge runs just north of Darkwhisper Gorge.",sec={{t="A Frozen Chasm of Ruins and Giants",b="Frostwhisper Gorge cuts through Winterspring's southern mountains, just north of Darkwhisper Gorge. Snow covers the ravine floor and cliff ridges, where stonework from ancient night elven settlements remains. Frostmaul giants and their preservers claim the gorge now. They fiercely defend its frozen crags, making travel into the ravine perilous.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Overlook",b="A narrow, quiet track leads to a small outpost atop the gorge's eastern cliffs. Travelers flying by wyvern or gryphon between Azshara, Orgrimmar, and Winterspring may spot it from above. An Ironforge banner marks the solitary dwarven camp at the cliff's edge. Crates of provisions, barrels of ale, a comfortable chair, and a rifle leaning against its rest sit there. The camp overlooks the drop to the Great Sea below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in Frostwhisper Gorge?",a="Frostmaul giants and Frostmaul Preservers inhabit the canyon floor and its surrounding terraces.",al={"monsters in frostwhisper gorge","what lives in frostwhisper gorge","frostwhisper mobs"}},{q="Where is Frostwhisper Gorge located?",a="Frostwhisper Gorge cuts through southern Winterspring's icy cliffs, just north of Darkwhisper Gorge.",al={"frostwhisper gorge location","where is frostwhisper gorge","frostwhisper map"}},{q="What is the small dwarf camp on the eastern cliffs?",a="A solitary dwarven campsite on the eastern ridge flies an Ironforge banner. It has a chair, a rifle, crates of provisions, and barrels of ale. The camp looks over the cliff toward the sea.",al={"dwarf camp winterspring","ironforge flag frostwhisper","eastern cliff camp"}},{q="Are there night elf ruins down in the gorge?",a="Yes. Ancient night elven pillars and stonework lie across the gorge floor and upper cliff ridges, remnants of old Kaldorei habitations.",al={"elven ruins frostwhisper","night elf architecture winterspring gorge"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="High on the chasm's eastern rim, a dwarf traveler has made camp. An Ironforge banner, a rifle, and plenty of ale are there, overlooking the ocean.",["race:NightElf"]="Ancient night elven structures lie in the gorge's snowy depths, where Frostmaul giants now prowl."},kw={"darkwhisper gorge","frostmaul","frostwhisper gorge","ironforge","winterspring"},rel={"subzone:darkwhisper-gorge","zone:winterspring","topic:night-elf","zone:ironforge","zone:azshara","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Frostwhisper Gorge"}}
E["subzone:hidden-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Hidden Grove",z="winterspring",s="Wild moonkin now guard the Hidden Grove in northeastern Winterspring.",h="Wild moonkin now guard the Hidden Grove in northeastern Winterspring.",sec={{t="A Secluded Sanctuary",b="Cliffs shelter the Hidden Grove from Winterspring’s bitter winds. Snow-dusted trees fill the sunken crater, nearly cut off from the world beyond. Its hidden rim is hard to reach. You must risk a steep drop or find a narrow cavern passage in the southeastern ridge.\n\nWhite hares once lived undisturbed in the valley. Now aggressive wild moonkin have taken the glade, and unwary travelers may be ambushed there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into the Hidden Grove?",a="The safest way into the Hidden Grove is through a concealed cave in the southeastern cliff face. You can scramble down the steep rim, but a fall could be fatal.",al={"how to enter hidden grove","hidden grove entrance","where is the cave"}},{q="What creatures live in the Hidden Grove?",a="Hostile wild moonkin now guard the Hidden Grove. Before they came, harmless white hares lived peacefully in the glade.",al={"what is in hidden grove","hidden grove mobs","who lives here"}},{q="Where in Winterspring is this grove located?",a="The Hidden Grove lies in far northeastern Winterspring, enclosed by towering stone cliffs.",al={"hidden grove location","where is hidden grove"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see the crater’s moonkin as wild nature turned fiercely defensive. Their presence may raise spiritual questions."},kw={"crater","hares","hidden grove","moonkin","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring"},src={"Hidden Grove"}}
E["subzone:ice-thistle-hills"] = {t="subzone",n="Ice Thistle Hills",z="winterspring",s="Ice Thistle yetis menace travelers southeast of Everlook. Snow covers the high hills, where a rugged cavern cuts through the slopes. The yetis claim the area and threaten anyone who leaves the main road.",h="Ice Thistle yetis menace travelers southeast of Everlook.",sec={{t="A Den of White Fur",b="At the heart of Ice Thistle Hills, a great cave cuts deep into the rock. Ice Thistle yetis hunt and make their nests there, roaming the rocky slopes and winding tunnels. Their territory lies near Everlook, putting goblin trade and visiting prospectors at risk. So travelers and traders hire hunters to cull the beasts for their thick pelts and pristine horns.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Ice Thistle Hills located?",a="Ice Thistle Hills lie in central Winterspring, directly southeast of Everlook, the goblin trading post.",al={"ice thistle hills location","where is ice thistle hills","yeti cave location"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="Ice Thistle yetis inhabit nearly all the hills’ slopes and the cavern. These white-furred brutes defend their territory fiercely.",al={"ice thistle monsters","what is in ice thistle hills","yeti types"}},{q="Why do adventurers hunt in the Ice Thistle Hills?",a="Travelers and tradesfolk in Everlook hire hunters to gather the yetis’ thick furs and pristine horns. These materials are prized for crafting and survival gear in the frigid valley.",al={"why kill yetis","yeti fur winterspring","ice thistle quest"}},{q="What resources can be gathered around the hills?",a="Icecaps grow on the outdoor slopes, and rich thorium veins lie deep within the yeti cave.",al={"herbs ice thistle","mining ice thistle cave"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The dark cavern burrowed into the hill is dangerous. Seasoned miners can find rich thorium veins there, guarded by yeti packs.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The freezing slopes around the hills are good ground for cold-weather plants such as Icecaps. Rare blooms sometimes grow near the cavern’s mouth."},kw={"everlook","ice thistle hills","ice thistle yetis","icecaps","pristine yeti horn","thick yeti fur","winterspring","yeti cave"},rel={"subzone:everlook","zone:winterspring"},src={"Ice Thistle Hills"}}
E["subzone:lake-kel-theril"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Kel'Theril",z="winterspring",s="Beneath Lake Kel'Theril's ice, ancient ruins hold the spirits of the kaldorei who once lived there. Snow and frozen water cover the remains of their outpost from before the Great Sundering.",h="Beneath Lake Kel'Theril's ice, ancient ruins hold the spirits of the kaldorei who once lived there.",sec={{t="A Frozen Tomb of the Highborne",b="Lake Kel'Theril lies frozen beneath Winterspring's bitter cold. Shattered pillars and arches rise through the ice and along the snowy banks. They are all that remains of Kel'Theril, an outpost of the ancient Highborne before the Great Sundering broke Kalimdor apart. Even in death, the fallen aristocracy found no rest. Their ghosts and specters still wander the lake, bound to the ruins of their former home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the lake haunted by night elves?",a="The spirits haunting Lake Kel'Theril are tormented ghosts of the ancient Highborne. When the Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart ten thousand years ago, their civilization collapsed. Their souls remain bound to the icy ruins of their settlement.",al={"lake keltheril ghosts","why are there spirits here","winterspring lake ghosts"}},{q="What ruins stand along the lake's shores?",a="The crumbling pillars and stonework along the lake belong to the Ruins of Kel'Theril. The ancient kaldorei settlement thrived under the Highborne before the War of the Ancients.",al={"ruins in the lake","what are the keltheril ruins"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Lake Kel'Theril's specters as a reminder of the ruin wrought by the ancient Highborne's arrogance."},kw={"highborne","kel'theril","lake kel'theril","ruins of kel'theril","specters","winterspring"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-kel-theril","zone:winterspring","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lake Kel'Theril"}}
E["subzone:mazthoril"] = {t="subzone",n="Mazthoril",z="winterspring",s="In central Winterspring, Mazthoril shelters the blue dragonflight in a vast cavern. Its ice tunnels are guarded by dragonkin, spell-wielding wyrms, and arcane sentries, and lead to the aerie of Haleh, the reclusive blue matriarch.",h="In central Winterspring, Mazthoril shelters the blue dragonflight in a vast cavern.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Blue Dragons",b="Just south of Everlook, Mazthoril is cut into the frozen mountains. A large brood lives within and answers to Malygos, the Spell-Weaver. Dragonkin patrol the cavern and the nearby crags, among them Spellmaw, Azurous, and General Colbatann.\n\nElite guardians keep watch over the inner caverns. The dragonspawn are attuned to raw arcane energy, so any journey inside is perilous without serious preparation.",sp=0},{t="The Teleportation Rune and the Matriarch",b="Deep in Mazthoril's frozen labyrinth, the drakes Manaclaw and Scryer watch a mystical rune set in the floor. Step on it, and it carries travelers to an isolated mountain aerie above the cavern.\n\nHaleh lives there, a blue dragon matriarch who keeps the guise of a high elf. Cautious toward mortals, she holds deep lore about draconic lineage and has a vital part in unlocking the hidden ward that protects Onyxia's Lair.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Mazthoril?",a="Haleh, a powerful blue dragon matriarch, oversees Mazthoril. She lives in an isolated aerie high above the cavern, reached through a magical rune deep in the tunnels. When greeting mortal visitors, she appears as a high elven woman.",al={"who leads mazthoril","who is the boss of mazthoril","mazthoril matriarch"}},{q="Why are blue dragons living in Winterspring?",a="The titans charged the blue dragonflight with guarding Azeroth's arcane magic. Its members watch lingering fonts of ancient energy across the world. Around Lake Kel'Theril, Winterspring holds remnants of the Highborne's ancient civilization, making Mazthoril a natural stronghold for the flight's sentinels in Kalimdor.",al={"why are there dragons in winterspring","why blue flight here","malygos brood winterspring"}},{q="How do you reach Haleh?",a="Fight through the dragonkin to the back of Mazthoril's inner cavern. Between the drakes Manaclaw and Scryer, a glowing arcane rune marks the floor. Step into its center to reach Haleh's high perch atop the mountain.",al={"reach haleh","get to haleh","teleport to haleh","where is haleh"}},{q="What role does Mazthoril play in entering Onyxia's Lair?",a="Alliance heroes investigating the protections around Onyxia's Lair are sent to consult Haleh. Her part in that journey is revealed in a hidden passage.",al={"onyxia key mazthoril","onyxia attunement haleh","drakefire amulet haleh"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes investigating the black dragonflight seek Haleh, the matriarch, in Mazthoril.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find Mazthoril compelling. Malygos's realm teems with creatures saturated in pure arcane power, drawing any scholar of the arcane."},kw={"blue dragonflight","colbatann","haleh","malygos","mazthoril","onyxia key","spellmaw","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","npc:onyxia","subzone:everlook","subzone:lake-kel-theril","topic:alliance"},src={"Mazthoril"}}
E["subzone:moon-horror-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Moon Horror Den",z="winterspring",s="In Winterspring’s mountains northeast of Everlook, raging owlbeasts defend their den. Travelers who draw near the icy cave mouth meet wildkin guarding their home.",h="In Winterspring’s mountains northeast of Everlook, raging owlbeasts defend their den.",sec={{t="A Den of Feathers and Frost",b="Moon Horror Den opens in the mountain northeast of Everlook. Raging owlbeasts live within, fierce and at home in Winterspring’s harsh snows. Winterfall Village lies south, but a sheer mountain face bars the way. The den remains an isolated refuge, far from the paths travelers take.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in the Moon Horror Den?",a="Raging owlbeasts live in Moon Horror Den. These large, aggressive wildkin are suited to Winterspring’s freezing climate, and they attack anyone who enters their cave.",al={"what is in moon horror den","moon horror den mobs","owlbeasts in cave"}},{q="Where is the Moon Horror Den located?",a="Moon Horror Den lies in eastern Winterspring, a short walk northeast of the goblin town of Everlook. Its mouth opens in the northern rock face.",al={"moon horror den location","how to find moon horror den","where is moon horror den"}},{q="Can you reach Winterfall Village from the den?",a="No. A high mountain ridge blocks the way south to Winterfall Village. To reach the village, you must go around the mountain slopes through the open valley.",al={"path to winterfall village","shortcut to winterfall","den to winterfall"}},{q="Why do travelers venture into this cave?",a="Travelers enter Moon Horror Den to hunt raging owlbeasts and help naturalists and researchers study Winterspring’s corrupted or aggressive wildkin.",al={"why go to moon horror den","moon horror den quests"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find the owlbeasts’ violent frenzy sobering. It reflects the wild turbulence gripping Winterspring.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face ferocious wildkin in the cave’s tight quarters. The thick-hided owlbeasts test your nerve up close."},kw={"cave","everlook","moon horror den","owlbeasts","raging owlbeast","wildkin","winterspring"},rel={"subzone:everlook","zone:winterspring","subzone:winterfall-village"},src={"Moon Horror Den"}}
E["subzone:owl-wing-thicket"] = {t="subzone",n="Owl Wing Thicket",z="winterspring",s="In southern Winterspring, berserk, moontouched, and crazed owlbeasts prowl the snowy crags of Owl Wing Thicket. Its caves and stone roosts hold ancient night elf altars tied to their origins and to Elune.",h="In southern Winterspring, berserk, moontouched, and crazed owlbeasts prowl the snowy crags of Owl Wing...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Moonkin",b="South of Everlook, Owl Wing Thicket is among Winterspring’s densest owlbeast nesting grounds. Long ago, night elf caretakers revered the creatures as sacred guardians blessed by Elune.\n\nAncient shrines and moonstone altars remain beneath the cavern overhangs. The lingering spirits of the Guardians of Elune watch over them. Many owlbeasts have fallen to madness and attack travelers who trespass in their holy hollows.",sp=0},{t="The Lore of the Moonkin",b="At Owl Wing Thicket, night elf scholars and priests seek communion with the Guardians of Elune. The priestess Ranshalla guides Alliance seekers as they light sacred braziers throughout the caves to awaken the ancient spirits.\n\nThe guardians tell how Elune first fashioned wild moonkin to protect pristine natural sanctuaries. Their words reveal the beasts’ divine ancestry, though many are now feral and hostile.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Owl Wing Thicket?",a="In southern Winterspring, Owl Wing Thicket’s snowy crags and caves shelter a dense population of wild owlbeasts. Ancient shrines there honor Elune, the night elf goddess.",al={"owl wing thicket","where is owl wing thicket","owl wing thicket lore"}},{q="Why are the owlbeasts here so aggressive?",a="Elune blessed the owlbeasts as protectors of nature, but many have fallen into violent frenzy. Berserk, moontouched, and crazed beasts roam Owl Wing Thicket and attack anyone who approaches their dens.",al={"why are moonkin mad","crazed owlbeasts winterspring","berserk owlbeasts"}},{q="Who is Ranshalla?",a="Ranshalla is a night elf priestess of Elune who journeys into Owl Wing Thicket. She seeks the ancient Guardians of Elune to learn the sacred origins and history of the moonkin.",al={"ranshalla","who is ranshalla winterspring","priestess ranshalla"}},{q="What are the Guardians of Elune found inside the thicket?",a="The Guardians of Elune are ancient night elf spirits tied to altars within the caves. Rekindling sacred fires summons them, and they tell how the moonkin were created to watch over wild and holy lands.",al={"guardians of elune","spirits in owl wing thicket","moonkin spirits"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Owl Wing Thicket is holy ground gone wild. Early accounts of Elune’s grace endure there beside feral moonkin that have lost their ancient balance.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold the owlbeast form sacred. Owl Wing Thicket is a sobering place, where creatures gifted with lunar affinity have fallen into unrestrained madness."},kw={"elune","guardians of elune","moonkin","moontouched","owl wing thicket","owlbeast","ranshalla","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Owl Wing Thicket"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-kel-theril"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Kel'Theril",z="winterspring",s="Snow and ice hold the broken stones of Ruins of Kel'Theril beside Lake Kel'Theril in central Winterspring. The ancient night elven city fell in the Great Sundering, and the spirits of its lost Highborne still haunt the ruins.",h="Snow and ice hold the broken stones of Ruins of Kel'Theril beside Lake Kel'Theril in central Winterspring.",sec={{t="A Shattered Legacy",b="Kel'Theril once stood among the great settlements of the ancient night elven empire. When the Well of Eternity collapsed in the Great Sundering, the city was blasted apart and buried beneath ice and snow. Its Highborne residents perished in the disaster, their souls bound to the stones. Now their spirits linger among the frostbitten arches, reliving their final moments.",sp=0},{t="Echoes in the Snow",b="Along Lake Kel'Theril, restless Highborne spirits haunt the ruined colonnades. Many are hostile, driven mad by millennia of isolation and the violent magic that tore their civilization apart. A few, including the Remorseful Highborne, seek travelers willing to hear their laments and help them make peace with their forgotten past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the city of Kel'Theril?",a="The Great Sundering destroyed Kel'Theril ten thousand years ago. When the Well of Eternity imploded and tore Kalimdor apart, the city collapsed into rubble and sudden bitter chill settled over Winterspring.",al={"kel'theril history","why is kel'theril ruined","how did kel'theril fall"}},{q="What spirits haunt these ruins?",a="The ruins are haunted by apparitions of Highborne night elves killed in the Great Sundering. Their souls remain bound to the fallen stones, trapped in agony as they wander the snowy shores of Lake Kel'Theril.",al={"kel'theril ghosts","who haunts kel'theril","kel'theril undead"}},{q="Can you speak with any of the ghosts?",a="Most of the spirits are hostile and lost to madness, but you can speak with a Remorseful Highborne among the ruins. The spirit will talk with Alliance travelers who seek to understand the site's tragic past.",al={"friendly ghost kel'theril","remorseful highborne","ghost quests kel'theril"}},{q="Where are the ruins located?",a="The ruins lie along the shores of Lake Kel'Theril in central Winterspring.",al={"kel'theril location","where is kel'theril","find kel'theril"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Kel'Theril as a solemn reminder of the ancient Highborne caste's arrogance and the devastation wrought by their reckless use of arcane magic.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can feel the dormant arcane energies that once sustained one of Kalimdor's proudest magic cities before the Sundering."},kw={"ghosts","highborne","kel'theril","lake kel'theril","ruins","sundering","winterspring"},rel={"subzone:lake-kel-theril","zone:winterspring","topic:highborne","topic:alliance","topic:druid"},src={"Ruins of Kel'Theril"}}
E["subzone:starfall-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Starfall Village",z="winterspring",s="Night elves shelter travelers at Starfall Village, the Alliance outpost on Winterspring’s snowy road. It offers supplies in the frozen valley and watches over a nearby barrow den.",h="Night elves shelter travelers at Starfall Village, the Alliance outpost on Winterspring’s snowy road.",sec={{t="An Alliance Refuge in the Snow",b="Northwest of Everlook and south of Frostsaber Rock, Starfall Village gives wayfarers shelter in Winterspring’s harsh mountain cold. Its timber lodges offer supplies and a warm hearth. The village is the Alliance’s only outpost in the valley, and a quiet barrow den nearby stands empty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Starfall Village?",a="Starfall Village is a night elven refuge in Winterspring and the Alliance’s main sanctuary in the valley. It offers lodging, trade, and guidance to scouts bound for Frostsaber Rock or looking into nearby barrow dens.",al={"starfall","starfall town","what is this place"}},{q="Can Horde players use the amenities in Starfall Village?",a="No. Starfall Village is held by the night elves and the Alliance. Horde travelers who come too close meet hostility from its defenders.",al={"is starfall friendly to horde","can horde use starfall","starfall village horde"}},{q="What is the barrow den next to the village?",a="The cavern directly behind Starfall Village is an empty barrow den. Barrows traditionally shelter druids while their spirits walk the Emerald Dream, but no druids sleep here.",al={"barrow den starfall","cave next to starfall"}},{q="Where is Starfall Village located?",a="Starfall Village sits along Winterspring’s main snow-covered road, northwest of Everlook and south of Frostsaber Rock.",al={"starfall location","how to get to starfall","where is starfall"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As the only Alliance settlement in Winterspring, Starfall Village offers vital respite, trade goods, and directions in the remote, treacherous highlands.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, Starfall is an important northern outpost beside a quiet, unoccupied barrow den."},kw={"alliance","night elf","starfall","starfall village","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","subzone:everlook","subzone:frostsaber-rock","topic:alliance"},src={"Starfall Village"}}
E["subzone:timbermaw-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Timbermaw Post",z="winterspring",s="Winterfall furbolgs hold Timbermaw Post in central Winterspring. The camp lies southeast across the road from Frostfire Hot Springs and west of Lake Kel'Theril.",h="Winterfall furbolgs hold Timbermaw Post in central Winterspring.",sec={{t="A Displaced Outpost",b="Winterfall furbolgs crowd Timbermaw Post in central Winterspring. You find the camp southeast across the road from Frostfire Hot Springs and west of frozen Lake Kel'Theril. Though it bears the Timbermaw name, the hostile Winterfall tribe controls the outpost. Demonic corruption has driven them mad and violent, and they press toward the central road.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Timbermaw Post if Winterfall furbolgs live here?",a="The corrupted Winterfall tribe controls the camp despite its name. No one knows its founding history.",al={"why timbermaw post","who owns timbermaw post","timbermaw post furbolgs"}},{q="Where is Timbermaw Post located?",a="Timbermaw Post lies in central Winterspring, southeast across the main road from Frostfire Hot Springs and directly west of Lake Kel'Theril.",al={"timbermaw post location","where is timbermaw post","timbermaw post map"}},{q="Are the furbolgs at Timbermaw Post hostile?",a="Yes. The furbolgs at Timbermaw Post belong to the hostile Winterfall tribe. Even if you have earned peaceful standing with the actual Timbermaw tribe, these furbolgs attack intruders on sight.",al={"are furbolgs here hostile","timbermaw post friendly","can i talk to timbermaw post"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid who reveres the furbolgs as ancient stewards of nature, you find the camp held by Winterfall furbolgs. The Burning Legion's lingering taint has driven them mad."},kw={"frostfire hot springs","furbolg","lake kel'theril","timbermaw","timbermaw post","winterfall","winterspring"},rel={"topic:furbolg","zone:winterspring","subzone:frostfire-hot-springs","subzone:lake-kel-theril"},src={"Timbermaw Post"}}
E["subzone:winterfall-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Winterfall Village",z="winterspring",s="In Winterfall Village, furbolgs have turned against travelers east of Everlook. Once peaceful kin to Kalimdor’s other ursine tribes, they now live in madness and violent corruption under High Chief Winterfall.",h="In Winterfall Village, furbolgs have turned against travelers east of Everlook.",sec={{t="A Tribe Consumed",b="Snowy terraces east of Everlook hold Winterfall Village, the main settlement of the Winterfall furbolgs in Winterspring. Like their cousins across northern Kalimdor, these bear-folk were warped and driven mad by the foulness left by the Burning Legion’s invasion.\n\nHigh Chief Winterfall leads the tribe from a secluded cavern atop the village’s highest tier. The furbolgs have abandoned their ancestral communion with the wild spirits of the snow. Now they assault travelers, patrol the mountain passes, and threaten anyone who comes near their frost-bitten home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Winterfall Village?",a="On snowy slopes east of Everlook in Winterspring, Winterfall Village is the main settlement of the Winterfall furbolgs.",al={"winterfall village info","what is this place","furbolg town winterspring"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="The Burning Legion’s lingering demonic taint warped the Winterfall furbolgs’ minds and drove them from peaceful customs to hostility toward outsiders after the Third War.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","corrupted furbolgs","why attack"}},{q="Who leads the village?",a="High Chief Winterfall leads the tribe from a small cave at the settlement’s highest point.",al={"who is the boss","winterfall leader","chief"}},{q="Why does Everlook care about this village?",a="Winterfall Village lies close to Everlook. Its furbolgs raid passing caravans, disrupt trade routes, and threaten the goblins’ mining and mercantile interests in eastern Winterspring.",al={"everlook goblins","why fight winterfall"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may mourn the Winterfall tribe’s corruption. Furbolgs were ancient allies of the night elves and the Cenarion Circle before demonic madness took hold.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may feel the Winterfall tribe’s fall as another painful break in the ancient bonds between your people and Kalimdor’s native peoples."},kw={"everlook","furbolg","high chief winterfall","winterfall","winterfall village","winterspring"},rel={"zone:winterspring","subzone:everlook","topic:furbolg"},src={"Winterfall Village"}}
E["zone:winterspring"] = {t="zone",n="Winterspring",z="winterspring",s="Snowstorms sweep Winterspring, where old dangers still shape life. High on Mount Hyjal's northeastern slopes, the valley lies above Moonglade and Felwood. Ancient Highborne ruins and fierce predators mark the land, while Everlook stands at its heart. Blue dragons shelter here, and demonic corruption grips the southern heights.",h="Snowstorms sweep Winterspring, where old dangers still shape life.",sec={{t="A Realm of Perpetual Frost",b="Snowstorms cross Winterspring's high forests, bluffs, and frozen lakes. Far below the summit, the valley rises above the surrounding wilds under cold mountain air. Vast roots of Nordrassil, the World Tree, arch through the drifts, twisted in the struggles of the Third War. Northern Kalimdor is mostly warm and thick with trees, but these alpine woods shelter frostsabers, chimaeras, yetis, and winter bears.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads and Outposts",b="Ancient passages through Timbermaw Hold link Winterspring with Felwood and Moonglade. Uncorrupted furbolgs guard the way and scrutinize travelers who pass through. At the valley's center, goblins of the Steamwheedle Cartel run Everlook, a trading town open to both Alliance and Horde. Its trade, engineering, and warm fires offer shelter from the mountain cold.",sp=0},{t="Old Ghosts and Blue Drakes",b="Kel'Theril's ruined pillars rise beside a frozen lake, haunted by the Highborne who once lived there. Reckless sorcerers shattered the cursed Crystal of Zin-Malor, and madness claimed them. Farther south, Mazthoril's caves hold the blue dragonflight's Kalimdor stronghold. Haleh, its matron protector, watches over Malygos's brood as they guard arcane currents and face nearby threats.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Shadow of the Gorge",b="Darkwhisper Gorge cuts through the calm at Winterspring's southern edge. Demonic forces left from the Third War crawl through its jagged canyons, blocking the high approaches to Mount Hyjal's summit. Winterfall furbolgs have also fallen to foul corruption. Independent researchers such as Donova Snowden investigate the spreading taint as it threatens the valley's wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Winterspring?",a="Winterspring lies beyond Timbermaw Hold, a network of tunnels in northeastern Felwood. The Timbermaw furbolgs attack travelers they judge hostile, so you must earn their trust to pass in peace. The eastern exit opens onto Winterspring's snowy slopes.",al={"getting to winterspring","how to enter winterspring","winterspring entrance","timbermaw tunnel winterspring"}},{q="Who runs the town of Everlook?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel runs Everlook. Its goblin traders keep the town neutral, so Horde and Alliance travelers may use its flight masters, repair vendors, banking vaults, and trade goods as long as they keep the peace.",al={"who controls everlook","everlook faction","is everlook neutral"}},{q="What are the ghosts haunting Lake Kel'Theril?",a="The ghosts are Highborne night elves who lived in Kel'Theril ten thousand years ago. Their sorcerers tampered with the stolen Crystal of Zin-Malor, and its shattering unleashed a curse that drove them mad. Centuries later, expeditions of high elves also fell to madness and now haunt the frozen ruins beside their ancestors.",al={"lake kel'theril ghosts","ruins of kel'theril spirits","who is at kel'theril"}},{q="Why are the Winterfall furbolgs aggressive?",a="The Winterfall furbolgs have fallen to a spreading, unnatural corruption that has driven their clan into maddened hostility. Nearby Timbermaw have kept their sanity, while dark influences hold the Winterfall. Researchers such as Donova Snowden study the taint and clear the clan's encampments.",al={"why are winterfall hostile","winterfall tribe corruption","donova snowden furbolgs"}},{q="What lives inside Mazthoril?",a="Mazthoril is the blue dragonflight's main roost and sanctuary on Kalimdor. Wyrmkin, elite whelps, and ancient drakes guard draconic relics and arcane secrets in its cavernous spires under Haleh's watch. She is the consort of the Aspect Malygos.",al={"mazthoril dragons","what is mazthoril","blue dragons in winterspring"}},{q="What is Darkwhisper Gorge?",a="Darkwhisper Gorge is a treacherous canyon at the valley's southern edge, held by powerful demons left from the Third War. They guard the dangerous trails leading toward Mount Hyjal's heights.",al={"darkwhisper gorge demons","what is in darkwhisper gorge","hyjal gate winterspring"}},{q="Can you train or tame frostsabers here?",a="At Frostsaber Rock in Winterspring's far north, the night elf Rivern Frostwind tends the native white cats. Help him secure provisions and protect the pride, and you may prove worthy of learning to rear and ride a Frostsaber.",al={"frostsaber mount","rivern frostwind frostsaber","how to get frostsaber"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Winterspring holds Icecap, an alpine herb found nowhere else, along with Mountain Silversage and rare Black Lotus. Alchemists seek Icecap for advanced concoctions.",["profession:Mining"]="Winterspring's icy crags and cavern walls yield Small and Rich Thorium Veins, as well as rare Truesilver deposits.",["race:NightElf"]="Winterspring carries deep ties to elven history. The Druids of the Talon rested for millennia in its barrow dens, Kel'Theril lies in ruins, and Nordrassil's exposed roots bear damage from the Battle of Mount Hyjal.",["class:Druid"]="High above Moonglade, Winterspring holds sacred meaning for druids. During the Third War, Malfurion Stormrage awakened the Druids of the Talon from their ancient sleep here.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes visit Rivern Frostwind at Frostsaber Rock to brave Winterspring's cold and earn the loyalty of the prestigious Winterspring Frostsaber mounts."},kw={"blue dragons","darkwhisper gorge","donova snowden","everlook","frostsaber","icecap","kel'theril","mazthoril","timbermaw","winterspring"},rel={"subzone:everlook","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:mazthoril","subzone:darkwhisper-gorge","subzone:ruins-of-kel-theril","subzone:frostsaber-rock","npc:donova-snowden","npc:rivern-frostwind"},src={"Winterspring (Classic)","Winterspring"}}
